<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Prout (Maryland)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">19th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Prout was a settler leader of the colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maryland">Maryland</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-palmas">Cape Palmas</a>, founded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maryland-state-colonization-society">Maryland State Colonization Society</a>. When the colony declared independence as the Republic of Maryland in 1854 he became its first governor; the republic was annexed by Liberia in 1857.</p></div>
